WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.310
- All right, let's wrap up this
hour with something awesome

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.080
I found scrolling through social media.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.136
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.136 --> 00:00:08.233
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.040
All hour we have celebrated
the value of a good book.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.860
Sadly, this country is seeing
the largest attack on books

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.430
in decades with more than
1,500 targeted for bans

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.070
in schools and libraries
just last last year.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.770
A Texas woman is fighting that
trend in a really cool way,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.490
opening a bookstore that focuses
on diversity and inclusion.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.620
And she also hosts a giant book club

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.410
featuring banned and challenged
books 'cause she's cool.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.610
We have her on the line right now

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.460
watching on KEYE TV in Austin.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.637
From Black Pearl Books,
everybody say hello to Katrina.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.010
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.850
Hi, Katrina.
- Hi, Kelly! How are you?

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.560
- I love it. I love having you on here.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.520
I love a fellow Texan.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.730
So this has been a lifelong
passion of yours, right?

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.080
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.570
So when my kids were
little, we'd always look

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.320
for books on representation,
diversity, inclusion.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.180
We'd talk about what they
were learning in school

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.730
and if it seemed like they
were only getting part

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.770
of the story, I'd always go to the library

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:09.390
or find books that allow for
the full story to be told.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.500
And so fast forward to 2019,
I started an online bookstore,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.420
and we helped popups and markets

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.120
to share those same
books with our community.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.180
And then in June of 2020

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.570
when the social justice movement happened,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.590
we had over 10,000 online
orders through our website,

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.210
which was just insane.
- Wow.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.210
- And we were operating out
of our home at the time.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.970
And so pallets of books were
being delivered to our house

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.010
and like, every square inch was covered

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.173
with the exception of our bedroom.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:44.430
Sales continued, and we had
to make some real decisions

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.920
for our family, and so
we stepped out on faith

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.470
and my husband left his corporate job

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.650
and came on board with me
to run the store full-time.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.740
And then last year we
moved into our storefront,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.570
and next time you're in Austin,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.010
we'd love for you to come visit.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.860
- Oh my gosh. Absolutely.
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.660
Absolutely, you put a lot of effort

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.580
into counteracting book bans as well.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.290
How did you do that?
- Yes.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.110
So unfortunately Texas leads the country

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:13.353
in the most banned books,
which is very, very sad.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.500
And I'm gonna use one
of your favorite words.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.710
We navigate the bowels of censorship

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:23.070
by starting a book club
called Redacted Reads,

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.098
and features books.

00:02:25.098 --> 00:02:28.590
We read fiction,
non-fiction, graphic novels,

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.720
young adult books, even children's books.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.150
And many of which you'd
actually be surprised

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.410
are on a banned book list.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.040
So of course the reasons
that they're banned vary.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.550
But it wouldn't come as a
surprise to you that the majority

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.400
of the books on the list have
some form of representation,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.103
be it Black, Indigenous,
Jewish, or LGBTQ+.

00:02:49.103 --> 00:02:52.140
To that end, we also started a nonprofit

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:57.060
called Put It In A Book, and
we have multiple initiatives

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.070
through that nonprofit that provide books

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.980
for hundreds of students
throughout our community.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.750
And the phrase "put it in a book"

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.030
comes from a not so great time in history

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.490
when Blacks were not
allowed to read or write.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.460
It was illegal, and if found
doing so, they were punished.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.770
So it was said that if
you wanna hide something

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.990
from a Black person, put it in a book.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.280
They'll never find it.
- Oh.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.640
- So we are claiming that
phrase, using it for good,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.960
and saying, hey, you gotta find
other places to hide things

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.910
because we do read, we do write,

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.001
and we do have stories to tell.

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:30.750
(audience cheers and applauds)
- Absolutely.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.250
It's so important what you're doing.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.086
Thank you so much, Katrina,
from one Texan to another.

00:03:35.086 --> 00:03:37.496
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:03:37.496 --> 00:03:39.433
(bell rings)
(audience applauding)

00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:41.460
- [Katrina] All right!
- And that's not all, ma'am.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.040
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.990
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.840
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.330
so they're gonna be
writing Put It In A Book

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.464
a check for $1,000, how's that sound?

00:03:53.464 --> 00:03:54.510
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.450
- (gasps) Oh, thank you! Thank you!

00:03:57.791 --> 00:03:59.640
- Absolutely, thank you so much, Katrina,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.260
for everything you're doing.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.670
Thanks to all our guests this hour,

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.460
Rachel McAdams, Judy
Blume, Abby Ryder Fortson,

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.080
Christine, and The Heavy.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.230
Y'all have a great day. If
it's not, try and change it.

